{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef sieve_primes(limit):\n    primes = []\n    for candidate in range(2, limit):\n        flag = True\n        for p in primes:\n            if p * p > candidate:\n                break\n            if candidate % p == 0:\n                flag = False\n                break\n        if flag:\n            primes.append(candidate)\n    return primes\n\nprimes = sieve_primes(6000)\n\ndef factorize(n):\n    result = {}\n    for p in primes:\n        if p * p > n:\n            break\n        if n % p == 0:\n            exponent = 0\n            while n % p == 0:\n                n //= p\n                exponent += 1\n            result[p] = exponent\n    if n > 1:\n        result[n] = 1\n    return result\n\ndef enumerate_divisors(n):\n    factorization = factorize(n)\n    divs = [1]\n    for prime, power in factorization.items():\n        temp = []\n        for d in divs:\n            p_val = 1\n            for _ in range(power + 1):\n                temp.append(d * p_val)\n                p_val *= prime\n        divs = temp\n    return divs\n\ndef solve(n, modulus):\n    dp = {0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 2}\n    for k in range(3, n + 1):\n        dp[k] = 2 * dp[k - 1]\n        for d in enumerate_divisors(k):\n            if 2 <= d <= k:\n                dp[k] += dp[k // d] - dp[(k - 1) // d]\n                dp[k] %= modulus\n        dp[k] %= modulus\n    return dp[n]\n\ndata = sys.stdin.readline().split()\nn_val = int(data[0])\nm_val = int(data[1])\nprint(solve(n_val, m_val))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <unordered_map>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvector<int> sieve_primes(int limit) {\n    vector<int> primes;\n    for (int candidate = 2; candidate < limit; candidate++) {\n        bool flag = true;\n        for (int p : primes) {\n            if (p * p > candidate) break;\n            if (candidate % p == 0) {\n                flag = false;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        if (flag) {\n            primes.push_back(candidate);\n        }\n    }\n    return primes;\n}\n\nvector<int> primes = sieve_primes(6000);\n\nunordered_map<int, int> factorize(int n) {\n    unordered_map<int, int> result;\n    for (int p : primes) {\n        if (p * p > n) break;\n        if (n % p == 0) {\n            int exponent = 0;\n            while (n % p == 0) {\n                n /= p;\n                exponent++;\n            }\n            result[p] = exponent;\n        }\n    }\n    if (n > 1) {\n        result[n] = 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nvector<int> enumerate_divisors(int n) {\n    auto factorization = factorize(n);\n    vector<int> divs = {1};\n    for (auto& kv : factorization) {\n        int prime = kv.first;\n        int power = kv.second;\n        vector<int> temp;\n        for (int d : divs) {\n            long long p_val = 1;\n            for (int i = 0; i <= power; i++) {\n                temp.push_back(d * p_val);\n                p_val *= prime;\n            }\n        }\n        divs = temp;\n    }\n    return divs;\n}\n\nint solve(int n, int modulus) {\n    unordered_map<int, int> dp;\n    dp[0] = 0;\n    dp[1] = 1;\n    dp[2] = 2;\n    \n    for (int k = 3; k <= n; k++) {\n        dp[k] = (2LL * dp[k - 1]) % modulus;\n        vector<int> divs = enumerate_divisors(k);\n        for (int d : divs) {\n            if (2 <= d && d <= k) {\n                dp[k] = (dp[k] + dp[k / d] - dp[(k - 1) / d]) % modulus;\n                if (dp[k] < 0) dp[k] += modulus;\n            }\n        }\n        dp[k] %= modulus;\n        if (dp[k] < 0) dp[k] += modulus;\n    }\n    return dp[n];\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_val, m_val;\n    cin >> n_val >> m_val;\n    cout << solve(n_val, m_val) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.376194530981593e-05, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.2636104656849056e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -6.23445157543756e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.00014411364099942148, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.182837463100441e-05, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -0.4756251573562622, -3.576272320060525e-06, -4.005352093372494e-05, -0.005929972976446152, -8.940656698541716e-06, -0.09448981285095215, -0.28115272521972656, -0.5760802626609802, -2.109982233378105e-05, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -0.0001333863037871197, -5.602820692729438e-06, -2.098061486321967e-05, -0.10034526139497757, -0.0004928089329041541, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -8.821448318485636e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.145764938177308e-06, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -3.099436753473128e-06, -9.179073458653875e-06, -1.5020257706055418e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -5.006777428206988e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.19209282445